  "notes": [
    "DESI-HVS1 (Gaia DR3 1323614710521141120; DESI DR1 target_id 39632956725136475): the authors retain it as an HVS candidate in the abstract and final summary (T:p1-b4; T:p7-b9). Its unbound status is marginal: the abstract gives P_ub ~ 50% (T:p1-b4), while Section 2.2 reports above 50% for the adopted galpy MWPotential2014 and around 30–40% for the other models/observational case (T:p3-b11). S5-HVS1 is only a literature comparison (T:p2-b0; T:p6-b5), and DESI-312 is explicitly described as bound (T:p6-b5); neither is treated as a target of this paper.",
    "DESI-HVS1: The paper reports V_GSR as a Galactocentric total velocity computed with two distance choices, so both values are retained. The unbound probability is potential-dependent and is given only as an approximate/inequality value for MWPotential2014 and as a 30–40% range for alternatives (T:p1-b4, T:p3-b11); no explicit bound probability is reported. The distance modulus is included under distance as reported (T:p5-b7)."
  ]
